/**
 * @mainpage cv-inference-server
 *
 * @tableofcontents
 *
 * @section mainpage_overview Overview
 *
 * **cv-inference-server** is a real-time computer-vision model serving system in
 * modern C++20, built as a portfolio project. It demonstrates the core building
 * blocks of a low-latency inference service:
 *
 * - a pluggable **backend abstraction** (`IInferenceBackend` + `FakeBackend`,
 *   with gated ONNX Runtime / TensorRT backends),
 * - **dynamic request batching** against a latency budget (`DynamicBatcher`),
 * - **fair compute scheduling** with backpressure (`Scheduler`),
 * - an **observability surface** (`MetricsRegistry`, Prometheus text + gated
 *   HTTP exposer), and
 * - a reproducible **benchmark harness** across compute paths (`cvis-bench`).
 *
 * @section mainpage_value Value proposition
 *
 * Serving CV models in real time is not just "call the model" -- it is coalescing
 * bursty concurrent requests into batches without blowing a latency budget,
 * dispatching those batches fairly across compute so no model starves, applying
 * backpressure instead of growing memory unbounded, and being able to *measure*
 * all of it reproducibly. The project implements that pipeline as clean,
 * independently testable C++20 modules that degrade gracefully from a GPU host
 * down to a CPU-only laptop.
 *
 * @section mainpage_status Feature status
 *
 * Capabilities fall into three honest buckets:
 *
 * - **Works on CPU-only / exercised in CI** -- core value types, the fake echo
 *   backend and backend factory, `DynamicBatcher`, `Scheduler`, `MetricsRegistry`,
 *   the `cvis-bench` CPU path, and the `cvis-server` core pipeline.
 * - **Present but flag-gated / GPU-only** -- the gRPC transport (`cvis_api`),
 *   ONNX Runtime / TensorRT backends, the Prometheus HTTP exposer, YAML/CLI
 *   config, and the CUDA/Vulkan benchmark cells.
 * - **Deferred** -- runtime model load/unload RPCs, GPU CI, the Vulkan compute
 *   path, and empirical latency baselining on hardware.
 *
 * See the top-level @c README.md for the full breakdown.
 *
 * @section mainpage_navigation Where to go next
 *
 * - @ref c4_components -- the C4 Component view of the running inference server
 *   process, with the real unidirectional layer dependencies.
 * - Module groups (one landing page per `cvis_*` library/executable):
 *   - @ref cvis_core
 *   - @ref cvis_backends
 *   - @ref cvis_batching
 *   - @ref cvis_scheduler
 *   - @ref cvis_metrics
 *   - @ref cvis_api
 *   - @ref cvis_runtime
 *   - @ref cvis_server
 *   - @ref cvis_bench
 *
 * The full design (interface signatures, concurrency model, rationale) lives in
 * `docs/design/architecture.md` and `docs/design/interfaces.md`; requirements are
 * in `docs/requirements/SRS.md`.
 */
